Howdy,

I seem to have hit my stride with Slash'em on my iPhone, having
finally gotten two different characters to their respective Quests.
I've documented the disappointment of having the Enforcer Quest fail
on me already; that character finally threw himself suicidally at
Vecna after having made it down as far as the Black Market.  (No magic
resistance means that even polymorphed into a ruby golem I only
survived about 6 turns.)

My latest character, a female droven Wizard, 13th level at time of
death, had done Sokoban, the Mines, Grund's, a Kobold level, and the
Neutral Quest.  She'd carefully avoided getting killed by the Chaotic
Quest, which is lethal when you have had zero genocides.  She'd
actually had a pretty easy run of things, other than having to kill
off a shopkeeper after he grabbed her backpack when she foolishly
tried to dig through his floor.  The Wizard Quest was tricky, mostly
due to having teleportitis but no teleport control, and having two
pods of nightgaunts spawned.  (Nearly killed by the tickle attack -
after that I killed them at long range.)  The Dark One is a punk; I
beat him to death with my hands.

When I found the Lawful Quest portal, I figured I'd clean out the
'easy' bits and leave the mind flayers (and lich) for after I got some
genocide ability.  I found an unidentified scroll in the rooms, but
was saving my identify scroll for the whole pile.  Unfortunately I
never finished the level, as I was killed from more or less max hit
points (99) in two-ish rounds by a rotworm + shade combination in the
twisty bits on the right side.  The first couple rotworms made me
deathly sick, which I healed right up with my horn, continuing on my
merry way.  As I encountered the next rot worm, I got some messages
indicating that I was being attacked by a shade (can't tell without
the messages, as it's just a dark spot like most of that area); the
messages also indicated a paralysis attack, which, after the
nightgaunts, I was wary of, so I immediately put a magic missile into
the shade, ignoring the rotworm.  And then I died.  The next attack by
the shade paralyzed me and it hit me until I died, while the rotworm
made me deathly ill.  I'm not sure what else I could have done, as
shades are difficult to detect and deal with at range, and I hit it as
quickly as I could with my most powerful attack.  Paralyzation is
perhaps a bit overpowered...

Anyone have any strategies for dealing with this threat?  I've never
had trouble with shades before; my enforcer cut them down trivially
with his 'saber, so I wasn't really prepared for one action, didn't
Elbereth = die.

